<!--
Scenario 10 - FALSE NEGATIVE: fast main-lane car (120 km/h) beyond ENTRY_ZONE_M=100 m

The merging car departs near the end of the entering ramp (departPos=1.83 on 954971261,
leaving only 20.4 m to the merge) so the detection trigger fires almost immediately (t~0).
At that moment the highway car is 140 m from the merge — just beyond ENTRY_ZONE_M
(100 m) — so the detector skips it.

At 120 km/h (33.3 m/s) the highway car reaches the merge in ~4.2 s.  The merging
car is still on the ramp.  This is a real collision risk that goes undetected.

Expected (ground truth): unsafe
Detector output:         safe  (false negative - ENTRY_ZONE_M too short)
Fix:                     increase ENTRY_ZONE_M from 100 m to at least 150 m

OSM edges:
  merging ramp : 954971261 (lane 0, accel) -> 106116297-AddedOnRampEdge -> 106116297
  highway main : 497720156 (lane 1, through) -> 353879480 -> ...-> 106116297

Merging car departPos=1.83 on 954971261:
  remaining in 954971261 = 16.44 - 1.83 = 14.61 m
  + 106116297-AddedOnRampEdge = 5.79 m → total 20.4 m to merge  (trigger fires ~immediately).

Main car 140 m before merge: 305.72 - 140 = 165.72 m into 497720156.
-->
<routes>
    <vType id="car" accel="2.6" decel="4.5" sigma="0.0" length="4.5"
           maxSpeed="40.0" minGap="2.5"/>

    <!-- Merging car starts 20.4 m from merge so trigger fires at t~0 -->
    <vehicle id="merging_car" type="car" depart="0.0"
             departLane="0" departPos="1.83" departSpeed="16.67">
        <route edges="954971261 106116297-AddedOnRampEdge 106116297"/>
    </vehicle>

    <!-- 140 m before merge: 305.72 - 140 = 165.72 -->
    <vehicle id="main_car" type="car" depart="0.0"
             departLane="1" departPos="165.72" departSpeed="33.33">
        <route edges="497720156 353879480 954971261 106116297-AddedOnRampEdge 106116297"/>
    </vehicle>
</routes>
